From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:17:06 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 94/96] Plutonium: a display added or removed while locked
 doesn't crash Ash

CloseWidgets() moved each lock widget out of widgets_ into DeleteSoon()
while hiding the rest. Hiding one could activate another window, and
OnWindowActivated() walked widgets_ through IsLockWindow(), dereferencing
the moved-from (null) entry. The widgets now leave widgets_ before any is
hidden.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../browser/ui/ash/main_extra_parts/plutonium_lock_impl.cc | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/ash/main_extra_parts/plutonium_lock_impl.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/ash/main_extra_parts/plutonium_lock_impl.cc
index d46cbd460c..d6cd682059 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/ash/main_extra_parts/plutonium_lock_impl.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/ash/main_extra_parts/plutonium_lock_impl.cc
@@ -405,13 +405,16 @@ void PlutoniumLockImpl::BuildWidgets() {
 
 void PlutoniumLockImpl::CloseWidgets() {
   view_ = nullptr;
-  for (auto& widget : widgets_) {
+  // Out of widgets_ first: hiding one can activate another window, and
+  // OnWindowActivated() walks widgets_ (a moved-from entry there crashed).
+  std::vector<std::unique_ptr<views::Widget>> widgets;
+  widgets.swap(widgets_);
+  for (auto& widget : widgets) {
     widget->Hide();
     // Not from inside one of the widget's own calls (the Enter key).
     base::SingleThreadTaskRunner::GetCurrentDefault()->DeleteSoon(
         FROM_HERE, std::move(widget));
   }
-  widgets_.clear();
 }
 
 void PlutoniumLockImpl::RebuildSoon() {
